{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage","id":800278,"title":"More options for prometheans not on a pilgrimage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-03T22:10:21-08:00","id":800278,"title":"More options for prometheans not on a pilgrimage?","content":"I'll start off by saying this for full disclosure: I was not a fan of 1st edition Promethean when it came out. I'm of the understanding that I overall wasn't in the minority in this, but I feel the need to begin by saying that. <br /> <br /> However, I'll also start off by saying that this is largely because of how much I really wanted to like it. I was amazingly excited when I heard about Promethean, and when I got the book, I did so already eager to make my first Promethean character. But the more I read of the book, the more I realized that it was... well... kind of broken... Thematically, mechanically, broken. I got the sense reading it that the 9 or so people on the writing staff had been working largely independently of each other and that no one was really communicating, because a lot of the ideas seemed fractured and half-realized, though still promising. Promethean was heart-breaking to me for the same reason the Star Wars prequels were heart-breaking to me, not because I thought it was horrendously bad (Not nearly as bad as most of the people around me seemed to think) but because I thought it was almost really, really good and then it wasn't.<br /> <br /> And that was heart-breaking to me, because more than any other line, I wanted Promethean to be good. <br /> <br /> The reason that I'm starting off by saying this is because as I read the teasers for the next Promethean books, I'm overall very pleased. Already, it seems like a lot of my major complaints and criticisms are being fixed and the game is, overall, getting much closer to the one I imagined in my head and became incredibly excited at the prospect of playing. I'm so incredibly happy about the bits and pieces that I've gotten to read.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That having been said, the one element of the game that I took the greatest umbrage with seems to not only still be present, but to have become an even larger and more inescapable element within the game. And in case you clicked on this without reading the title, and I'm not sure why you did that, it's the pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't think the pilgrimage is a bad idea. In fact, I think it's a great idea, to a point. What I didn't like about it was its implementation: that every single promethean was on one and trying to become human. And by and large, the ones that weren't were lunatics and freaks. <br /> <br /> I get that Promethean is a game about trying to become human. I just don't think it should be. I think giving it that incredibly narrow focus is missing out on a lot of the potential inherent in the concept. You're a creature which shouldn't be. Your creation and your existence are both unnatural. Reality itself hates you for existing. How do you react to that? What kind of existence do you try to carve out? Trying to &quot;fix&quot; it and become human is one potential idea, absolutely. And it should be represented in the rules. But there are plenty of other ways to explore that concept. Maybe your character sees the power at his disposal and decides to use it. Maybe, even recognizing how much it sucks being what she is, the thought of trying to become something else scares her or makes her uncomfortable. Maybe he even rejects the idea that he &quot;shouldn't be&quot; and, rather than apologizing for his own existence, decides to live out a kind of defiance and try to make a life for himself as he is.<br /> <br /> As it stands, all of those concepts have to be played out as a centimani, who are canonically more or less all crazy.<br /> <br /> And from the bits of 2e I've gotten to see, it only looks like the pilgrimage has become a more inescapable aspect of the game in its mechanics, and that the centimani have only become even more resistant to being player character concepts.<br /> <br /> This is all a prelude to asking if there is any talk at all of giving any kind of options to players who want to play a promethean, but don't want to then spend their game trying to become a squishy human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T22:48:27-08:00","id":800290,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here\">We did this thread already</a>. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/316262-the-freaks-come-out-at-night-centimani-open-dev\">Multiple times.</a><br /> <br /> The only new thing you've brought to the table is that your argument leans on a thematic aspect that's explicitly been deemphasized in Second Edition and somehow completely ignored the pre-established fact that overwhelming majority of the overwhelmingly small number of Created are not satisfied with the state of their existence even without the matters of Disquiet and the Wasteland.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/532418-some-thoughts-on-the-humanism-vs-transhumanism-debate-in-promethean?p=533586#post533586\">You're on fire.</a> &quot;Burn down regardless&quot; doesn't need more mechanical teeth than &quot;play while ignoring the Pilgrimage and deal with the consequences.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T23:08:52-08:00","id":800302,"title":"","content":"&quot;I want a to ignore the core premise of the game&quot; isn't a thread topic that'll get you anywhere, OP. The Created are either on the Pilgrimage, stagnant, or actively regressing; the journey to become human is what defines them more than anything else. Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Hunter... these are games with a wide variety of story options; Promethean exists to tell stories about humanity through the lens of imitating it. It's an interatice art piece as much as it is an RPG.<br /> <br /> If that doesn't interest you, that's fine, but it just means Promethean isn't the game for you. Don't try to force it into something it isn't, and don't start threads that have been done to death already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T23:26:10-08:00","id":800306,"title":"","content":"What the others said. Let's put this subject down in the grave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T23:39:23-08:00","id":800310,"title":"","content":"Overall, I don't think you're going to end up satisfied on this front. Promethean is about the Pilgrimage. It's at the center of the game and pretty much always has been. As Matt's said, the Pilgrimage is the buy-in for Promethean, the hook that you start with and look for interest in. If you're not interested in the Pilgrimage? Hey, not a problem, everybody's got different tastes. But yours aren't gonna include Promethean. Same way that you don't dig into Vampire if you're not interested in moral ambiguity and compromises to sustain yourself, or Demon if you don't want a game of lies and counterintelligence.<br /> <br /> But some individual responses:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage#post800278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the pilgrimage is a bad idea. In fact, I think it's a great idea, to a point. What I didn't like about it was its implementation: that every single promethean was on one and trying to become human. And by and large, the ones that weren't were lunatics and freaks.<br /> <br /> As it stands, all of those concepts have to be played out as a centimani, who are canonically more or less all crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know everything that's planned for second edition, but as I've always understood it, not every Promethean on the Pilgrimage knows he's on the Pilgrimage. There are many roads to the dawn and a lot of lessons to be learned, and many of those aren't about overtly studying humans and learning their ways. The limits of the Refinement of Gold are that you can't force your way into a lot of understandings about personhood. Many of them can't be found until you stop looking for them.<br /> <br /> The constants, I think, are a hollow, gnawing feeling in the Promethean's gut: the Azoth has enough self-awareness to recognize that it doesn't belong, even before the world starts actively rejecting it. It has an instinctive drive to complete itself. If you know there's something awry, and you're trying to set it right, be better and grow? You're probably on the Pilgrimage in some sense. You might not be able to elucidate a Refinement or identify an end-point to this self-completing drive, but you're still able to progress toward it, even very slowly and haltingly. It still counts. The Hundred-Handed aren't just stalled on the Great Work. They're not just Prometheans who feel they have a right to live in this world. They're Prometheans who feel that gnawing hole deep within their selfhood and stretch it wider. They know they can be something more whole, something healthier, and they choose to run in the opposite direction. That's what's self-destructive about it.<br /> <br /> I think there are some weaknesses in the game \u2013<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage#post800278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it stands, all of those concepts have to be played out as a centimani, who are canonically more or less all crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2013 including that the Centimani we're presented with are flatter than what the concept as a whole describes, and also that there's probably more that orthodox Metamorphosis ought to be able to do with the Promethean body that doesn't reflect the chaotic breakdown of Pandoran Transmutations (gross shouldn't be the same as self-destructive). But I don't think all Prometheans are supposed to either be consciously, explicitly trying to transmute themselves into mortal humans or be Centimani. If you don't know what would put the capstone on your Great Work, or are following some alternate idea of it, you probably won't be taking the final step into the New Dawn as is. But that doesn't mean you aren't better preparing yourself for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage#post800278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're a creature which shouldn't be. Your creation and your existence are both unnatural. Reality itself hates you for existing. How do you react to that? What kind of existence do you try to carve out? Trying to &quot;fix&quot; it and become human is one potential idea, absolutely. And it should be represented in the rules. But there are plenty of other ways to explore that concept. Maybe your character sees the power at his disposal and decides to use it. Maybe, even recognizing how much it sucks being what she is, the thought of trying to become something else scares her or makes her uncomfortable. Maybe he even rejects the idea that he &quot;shouldn't be&quot; and, rather than apologizing for his own existence, decides to live out a kind of defiance and try to make a life for himself as he is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being something awful and wrong but trying your best to use that nature to good ends is one of the cores of Vampire, and to varying extents, all the WoD games. Being defiant and telling the world that no matter how terrible you may be, it's your nature and you don't need to apologize for it is Beast.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Promethean shouldn't have room for ideas like that. I think a lot of Prometheans who think they're stalled out on the Pilgrimage might still be progressing while trying to do some good with the Divine Fire they've been given. I'm more saying, a game gets its identity by staking out some position on what it is and means, beyond the aesthetics of whether you're a shaggy wolfman or a lumpy frankenstein. If you try to run in every direction at once you stretch yourself thin. Maybe Promethean could use a little more thought to exception cases, the way Vampire occasionally has mystic hermits trying to unlive in relative seclusion and peace, and Werewolf has the occasional lone wolf character without the camaraderie and structure of a dedicated pack. But it still won't be about those things as much as it's about the Pilgrimage, because that's the core pitch.<br /> <br /> A second edition can make a lot of changes, but it's seldom expected to swerve the core pitch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T23:53:17-08:00","id":800314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800310#post800310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying Promethean shouldn't have room for ideas like that. I think a lot of Prometheans who think they're stalled out on the Pilgrimage might still be progressing while trying to do some good with the Divine Fire they've been given. I'm more saying, a game gets its identity by staking out some position on what it is and means, beyond the aesthetics of whether you're a shaggy wolfman or a lumpy frankenstein. If you try to run in every direction at once you stretch yourself thin. Maybe Promethean could use a little more thought to exception cases, the way Vampire occasionally has mystic hermits trying to unlive in relative seclusion and peace, and Werewolf has the occasional lone wolf character without the camaraderie and structure of a dedicated pack. But it still won't be about those things as much as it's about the Pilgrimage, because that's the core pitch.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really more what I'm trying to say. I don't want the pilgrimage taken out, but I think it's stifling to expect every player character to be shoved into this singular funnel. Werewolf has ghost wolves and such. But Promethean doesn't really have any options for the guy who wants to play a frankenstein monster and doesn't want to be sent along this specific path. <br /> <br /> As far as other responses are concerned, I'm sorry, but I admit I don't stalk the forums as much as others, perhaps. I come on here once in a blue moon, when I have a question or some such, but I did not know this was a topic that had been discussed at length before, and I apologize for digging it out of its grave, so to speak. (Though I'd argue the fact that it has been brought up numerous times only serves to reinforce my point.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T00:03:41-08:00","id":800318,"title":"","content":"My group looks at 1ed P:tC the same way someone described playing an Abyssal in Exalted: You're either Killshit McSoulfucker, or Mr. I-Don't-Want-To-Play-This-Splat-Anymore. I gotta say, not great choices. No one at my table is immune to the power fantasies inherent in all RPGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T00:06:32-08:00","id":800320,"title":"","content":"It's been brought up numerous times; it's been shouted down as fundamentally against the core premise of the game each and every time, by fans, writers, and developers.<br /> <br /> The Pilgrimage is just as essential to Promethean as &quot;playing a frankenstein monster&quot; if not more so, and if you don't like that... you're looking at the wrong game. I don't know what else you expect from this thread beyond that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T00:17:59-08:00","id":800335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800314#post800314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's really more what I'm trying to say. I don't want the pilgrimage taken out, but I think it's stifling to expect every player character to be shoved into this singular funnel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Growing up isn't a funnel unless you have issues with causality or a coherent sequential experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolf has ghost wolves and such. </div> </div> </div>Non sequitur. The degree to which Ghost Wolves (there is no &quot;and such&quot;) are addressed is roughly proportional to the amount of space given to non-Centimanus divergences from &quot;completing the Pilgrimage means becoming human&quot; in 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Promethean doesn't really have any options for the guy who wants to play a frankenstein monster and doesn't want to be sent along this specific path. </div> </div> </div>Too much specificity is being assumed in what &quot;become human&quot; or &quot;gain a soul&quot; means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Though I'd argue the fact that it has been brought up numerous times only serves to reinforce my point.) </div> </div> </div>Your point is that you don't like the base game or the fact that the base game does not overtly support divergences from the base game that amount to &quot;run the game without the inbuilt plotting skeleton.&quot;<br /> <br /> Other topics that have been brought up too many times on these forums include &quot;the True Fae of Changeling: the Lost are aware that they are fictional characters in a storytelling game in a manner that breaks the fourth wall,&quot; &quot;I am incapable of seeing past the mechanistic aesthetics of Demon: the Descent or connecting same to a longstanding history of tying the Divine Plan to machinery, therefore DtD is not about demons&quot; and &quot;Why can't my character in Mummy: the Curse, a game whose characters are the ritually preserved remnants of a precursor ancient-Egyptian empire, be white or from another culture that had things we call mummies?&quot;<br /> <br /> The persistence of a faulty notion does not give it credence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T00:25:17-08:00","id":800349,"title":"","content":"Satchel, you're giving me some pretty painful flashbacks there with the Mummy and Demon things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T00:34:42-08:00","id":800357,"title":"","content":"I think you are playing up too much the restrictions of the pilgramige while downplaying the restrictions of other games. A Ghost Wolf doesn't have to join a pack but a wolf who doesn't hunt is going to be a crazy broken thing. A vampire doesn't have to play into Vampire society but one who rejects basic human interaction is going to be heading into full on wassail. A mage who rejects their obsessions is going to be pretty messed up and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> Conversely the Pilgramage is just &quot;Do stuff&quot;. your character might be metaly moving towards a goal but that's not the case for what he knows. Yes, you can't take the concepts you want to play forever, but a Ghost wolf who rejects packs tries not to do anything wolfy at all and yells at all the other pcs for daring to try and make a proper Uratha out of him is.. well a shit character. The Ghost wolf who starts out rejecting everything is going to be forced by the general conceits of the game to accept territory and probably the pack. Your character concepts work pretty well on a number of other refinements but the conceit of promethean is they will learn that they are wrong. That change is needed. That no they can't do more good than harm and yes the world really does hate you. But those can be WHOLE chronicles by themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T00:54:51-08:00","id":800368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800357#post800357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you are playing up too much the restrictions of the pilgramige while downplaying the restrictions of other games. A Ghost Wolf doesn't have to join a pack but a wolf who doesn't hunt is going to be a crazy broken thing. A vampire doesn't have to play into Vampire society but one who rejects basic human interaction is going to be heading into full on wassail. A mage who rejects their obsessions is going to be pretty messed up and so on and so forth.<br /> <br /> Conversely the Pilgramage is just &quot;Do stuff&quot;. your character might be metaly moving towards a goal but that's not the case for what he knows. Yes, you can't take the concepts you want to play forever, but a Ghost wolf who rejects packs tries not to do anything wolfy at all and yells at all the other pcs for daring to try and make a proper Uratha out of him is.. well a shit character. The Ghost wolf who starts out rejecting everything is going to be forced by the general conceits of the game to accept territory and probably the pack. Your character concepts work pretty well on a number of other refinements but the conceit of promethean is they will learn that they are wrong. That change is needed. That no they can't do more good than harm and yes the world really does hate you. But those can be WHOLE chronicles by themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a large extent, I'd agree with you. Where I'd argue with that is on 3 points. (More like 2 and half, though)<br /> <br /> Point the first, the examples you point out are fluff/world examples that would be enforced by the story-teller. They largely aren't built into the mechanics of the game. Nothing in the mechanics rulebook says that the society-eschewing vampire or the ghost wolf are going to get screwed over and have to fall into line eventually. That's a consequence of the world that is portrayed in the books, and it's up to the story-teller and the player whether to integrate that into their campaign and let that be a force that the character has to deal with eventually. Promethean, however, has that aspect built into the mechanics of the game. If you want to ignore the pilgrimage, the rules of the game fight you on it.<br /> <br /> And this leads me to my second (half) point. You can, for sake of example, play vampire as a hack and slash game. It's not the way the game was meant to be played and, I'd argue, it's a terrible idea to try to play it that way. The rules are designed for narrative-heavy games, where combat is an afterthought, there to help a narrative progress, but intentionally kept light so those combats don't bog down the narrative. But the game won't stop you from running it that way. The games all have certain ways you're *intended* to play them, but you're allowed to ignore the fluff at your leisure to play them in different ways. Promethean doesn't give you that option, though. The pilgrimage is built into the mechanics of how prometheans work.<br /> <br /> 3rd point, the ghost wolf who goes out of his way not to be a proper uratha IS a shit character... for a game of werewolf. For a crossover game, he's actually a lot easier to integrate than anything else. nWoD/CoD is supposed to be super-modular, with it being possible to run different splats in the same game. The major difficulty in this is that the different games all have indivdual themes they're meant to explore, and these don't combine well. This is where it's insanely useful to have characters who reject those themes. Unaligned vampires, ghost wolves, and the like are much easier to integrate into a game that doesn't stick with any individual splat. A promethean trying to become human has no motivation to hang out with a changeling, a sin-eater, and a vampire. Hanging out with non-humans will, at best, do nothing for that goal, and may even hamper it, if he's following Aurum or something. A promethean with his own goals is easier to justify doing that, just like a ghost wolf requires way fewer mental gymnastics to explain why he'd want to hang out with that group than a blood talon or a hunter in darkness who's got a pack that he has to run with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T01:04:53-08:00","id":800374,"title":"","content":"I know it's probably will be a slight flame war, but I made non-canon answer to the problem &quot;not all prometheans should pursue Pilgrimage&quot; I myself have. It's in no way official POV, but it let me to enjoy <b>Promethean: the Created </b>as written. It's just let me play it without inner cringe on forcing the Pilgrimage in it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=318790#post318790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that transhuman Created are popular, in great numbers. Or that they truly <b>are right</b>. They are just giving other answer to the question &quot;What should I do with mine existence?&quot; compared to classical seeking New Dawn Prometheans. I think they object in the game will only add to the setting - they are those that don't agree with typical PCs and <b>neither</b> of sides can't tell they are absolute right. Redemption seeking Prometheans will argue that universe favors them - and even Principle is supporting they quest. &quot;Transhuman&quot; Created will point that New Dawn is taking it's toll on you, and you giving up powers and knowledge you were collecting in previous life. Why would you need this if this should be Prize, after all years of Pilgrimage?<br /> <br /> Both sides are correct, and it's only to players and their characters to decide. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/317752-promethean-and-transhumanism-goes-here?p=317933#post317933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can, just like I pointed before - in posthuman state, Uplifted dolphines or chimpanzee <i>were</i> never humans. But still they will be posthumanity, joining the new kind of humanity with they thoughs or personas.<br /> <br /> The problem with Centimani is that isn't looking for transhumanity in itself - <b>maybe</b> a posthumanity, but in my eyes, most of it is &quot;I need any possible power, and will destroy universe to get it&quot;. They seed Flux, unmaking the reality itself, just to get an edge on those around you. It's not transhumanity, it's <b>anti</b>-humanity, like it was stated in their post topic.<br /> <br /> The true transhuman Refinements are probably Argentum, Ferrum and Plumbum. First is analyzing those that suppress humans in some way ( other supernaturals of WoD ). Second is about physical and mental might, naturally leading to evolution of this particular specimen of Created. Last one is not looking on humanity as particular template, but on Created themselves, wanting to analyze their of kind - and maybe fixing they own &quot;curses&quot;, like Torment, or Disfigurments.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem the transhumanistic Created would have is the need to end they Pilgrimage as humanity - even if, in some way, New Adam is better than humans. The main problem of them is that they have those &quot;curses&quot; that are problems, not they supernatural strengths or long lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, transhumanistic prometheans have their harder because the universe try to push them on the Pilgirmage. But they still could try to resist it. There are ways to &quot;cheat&quot; the Pilgrimage to move you on and on... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 01-04-2016, 04:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T01:14:55-08:00","id":800377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800368#post800368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in the mechanics rulebook says that the society-eschewing vampire or the ghost wolf are going to get screwed over and have to fall into line eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Ghost Wolf who ignores the Shadow and the Hunt is eventually going to become a berserker cannibal and a vampire who doesn't have some basic tie to humanity and/or a means of getting a lot of Vitae is going to get dragged down into torpor in short order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Promethean, however, has that aspect built into the mechanics of the game. If you want to ignore the pilgrimage, the rules of the game fight you on it. </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to name some specific points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Promethean doesn't give you that option, though. The pilgrimage is built into the mechanics of how prometheans work. </div> </div> </div>There are methods of getting Vitriol outside the context of milestones and Second Edition has made non-nomadic play <i>more </i>sustainable thanks to the changes in how Disquiet works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> nWoD/CoD is supposed to be super-modular, with it being possible to run different splats in the same game. The major difficulty in this is that the different games all have indivdual themes they're meant to explore, and these don't combine well. This is where it's insanely useful to have characters who reject those themes. Unaligned vampires, ghost wolves, and the like are much easier to integrate into a game that doesn't stick with any individual splat. A promethean trying to become human has no motivation to hang out with a changeling, a sin-eater, and a vampire. </div> </div> </div>And here we run into the crux of the problem: with the exception of Beast, none of the games are built with crossover viability as a <i>draw</i>, and mislabeling characters who aren't assumed to be integrated into the political structures of their respective lines as &quot;rejecting [their line's] themes&quot; doesn't scan as an argument for &quot;most Promethean characters in the setting being inclined to gradually move towards getting a soul and becoming human is preventing me from running a less goal-driven game.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T01:22:21-08:00","id":800381,"title":"","content":"OTOH, there's always Argentum\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T01:25:22-08:00","id":800382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800381#post800381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OTOH, there's always Argentum\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of which, I wonder what the Roles for that are going to be like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T01:33:19-08:00","id":800386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800377#post800377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Ghost Wolf who ignores the Shadow and the Hunt is eventually going to become a berserker cannibal and a vampire who doesn't have some basic tie to humanity and/or a means of getting a lot of Vitae is going to get dragged down into torpor in short order.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The wolf must hunt. He doesn't need to throw his hat in with the forsaken or the pure. He can ignore the shadow to a certain extent. A vampire needs blood. He doesn't really need to join a covenant or bother with vampiric politics. He can totally eschew vampiric society to focus on mortal interests and goals that appealed to him in life and continue to do so. He might get bored with it after a while, but that's that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're going to have to name some specific points.<br /> <br /> <br /> Biggest one that comes to mind: Your refinement is the specific path you are taking to getting a soul. It also determines which transmutations you have an affinity for, and there's really no way to begin play without one. I mean, I suppose nothing's stopping you, but the book doesn't really give you any indication of what transmutations you start with, if you have any kind of affinity for any, or answers to a lot of other questions that pop up when you consider doing so. And what I've seen of 2E doesn't look poised to change that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There are methods of getting Vitriol outside the context of milestones and Second Edition has made non-nomadic play <i>more </i>sustainable thanks to the changes in how Disquiet works.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You are correct on both counts, and these are changes I'm quite happy about. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And here we run into the crux of the problem: with the exception of Beast, none of the games are built with crossover viability as a <i>draw</i>, and mislabeling characters who aren't assumed to be integrated into the political structures of their respective lines as &quot;rejecting [their line's] themes&quot; doesn't scan as an argument for &quot;most Promethean characters in the setting being inclined to gradually move towards getting a soul and becoming human is preventing me from running a less goal-driven game.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> True, they aren't a &quot;draw,&quot; but it's still supposed to be viable. That was a big advertisement when nWoD came about since crossovers were notoriously difficult in the OU. I'm not saying that not integrating into a political structure is rejecting the line's theme, persay. What I am saying is that it's a step towards creating a character who isn't tied to those specific themes, because those political structures are also pretty intrinsically tied into those themes. An unaligned vampire shows a distinct lack of interest in vampiric society. It's easier to understand why he may be interested in chumming it up with a changeling. And vice-versa, because the changeling probably won't want to hang out with a guy whose main interest is manipulating a power structure that he doesn't care about. And neither of those guys really understand or care about pangea and they likely wouldn't have much motivation to lock arms with a guy who's all &quot;we have to patrol the gauntlet you guys!&quot;<br /> <br /> And even still, I think you're missing my core point here, which is not that other splats can opt not to join their social group options. It's that it's exceedingly hard to come up with any reason why my created would, while trying to pursue the understanding of humanity, would be drawn to spending his time with a bunch of creatures which are decidedly not human. If he's given up on that goal, it makes more sense why he'd want to do that. But if the only option for the guy who's given up on that goal is a batshit centimani, then it becomes a question of why any of those guys would wanna hang out with the 8-armed lunatic cackling like a maniac.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T01:35:08-08:00","id":800387,"title":"","content":"Like I said: Argentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T01:38:02-08:00","id":800390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800368#post800368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To a large extent, I'd agree with you. Where I'd argue with that is on 3 points. (More like 2 and half, though)<br /> <br /> Point the first, the examples you point out are fluff/world examples that would be enforced by the story-teller. They largely aren't built into the mechanics of the game. Nothing in the mechanics rulebook says that the society-eschewing vampire or the ghost wolf are going to get screwed over and have to fall into line eventually. That's a consequence of the world that is portrayed in the books, and it's up to the story-teller and the player whether to integrate that into their campaign and let that be a force that the character has to deal with eventually. Promethean, however, has that aspect built into the mechanics of the game. If you want to ignore the pilgrimage, the rules of the game fight you on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harmony and Humanity will fuck you over, Its right there in the mechanics. Wolves and Vampires have it worse than Prometheans at least centimari can get back on the road. You don't come back from Wassail or permanently becoming a spirit and too many breaks toward Flesh will you pretty much full on crazy and unplayable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And this leads me to my second (half) point. You can, for sake of example, play vampire as a hack and slash game. It's not the way the game was meant to be played and, I'd argue, it's a terrible idea to try to play it that way. The rules are designed for narrative-heavy games, where combat is an afterthought, there to help a narrative progress, but intentionally kept light so those combats don't bog down the narrative. But the game won't stop you from running it that way. The games all have certain ways you're *intended* to play them, but you're allowed to ignore the fluff at your leisure to play them in different ways. Promethean doesn't give you that option, though. The pilgrimage is built into the mechanics of how prometheans work. </div> </div> </div>Yes i can cut out humanity and have an awkward but playable vampire. It excises a pretty major chunk of the themes of the book and a pretty major amount of the pages. But if I want to do that with Vampire.. I can do that with Promethean. Hack and slash Promethean made simple. Drop humanity. Drop Disquiet. Drop Wastelands. Refinements are now &quot;What i think is really cool so I will go adventure about&quot; Ok done. And no more of a break than dropping humanity from vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3rd point, the ghost wolf who goes out of his way not to be a proper uratha IS a shit character... for a game of werewolf. For a crossover game, he's actually a lot easier to integrate than anything else. nWoD/CoD is supposed to be super-modular, with it being possible to run different splats in the same game. The major difficulty in this is that the different games all have indivdual themes they're meant to explore, and these don't combine well. This is where it's insanely useful to have characters who reject those themes. Unaligned vampires, ghost wolves, and the like are much easier to integrate into a game that doesn't stick with any individual splat. A promethean trying to become human has no motivation to hang out with a changeling, a sin-eater, and a vampire. Hanging out with non-humans will, at best, do nothing for that goal, and may even hamper it, if he's following Aurum or something. A promethean with his own goals is easier to justify doing that, just like a ghost wolf requires way fewer mental gymnastics to explain why he'd want to hang out with that group than a blood talon or a hunter in darkness who's got a pack that he has to run with. </div> </div> </div><br /> Just.. no? The Pilgramige isn't the equivalent of being a Ghost WOlf or Unaligned. Its the Equivalent of &quot;Does Vampire/werewolf things&quot;. A werewolf who want to hang out with vampires and mages and hunt shit? Perfectly playable. One who wants to just be a normal person and doesn't want to do anything wolfy? Mechanics will hammer him hard. An unaligned Vampire who wants to go reenact Being Human? Perfectly playable. One who wants to go around murdering people by the truckload? Not so much. Honestly a Tribed Wolf who's decided &quot;this random bunch of misfits are my pack&quot; makes more sense with current mechanics than &quot;I want ot completely opt out&quot;<br /> <br /> As for the Promethean, You are really over thinking stuff. The path to humanity is like having a Shadowrun character who's goal is &quot;Retire to myown private island&quot; but instead of being about getting money its about getting milestones. You get enough milestones you get to retire your character, you don't want to retire your character when you hit x? ask the ST to make it X+10. &quot;But my character thinks he's ok like he is&quot; Is he growing as a character and changing as a person? Pilgrimage. &quot;My character is afraid of the new dawn&quot; Are they growing as a person and developing as a character. Pilgrimage. &quot;My character raises a fist in defiance against the world for daring to say I shouldn't exist&quot; Sounds like a great Refinement of Tin concept to me. Yeah.. eventually they have to deal with their central character concept in.. order to retire as a character.<br /> <br /> Promethean 1e had 10 refinements, 2e will have 12 I believe. Here's how it will generally go &quot;Hey st I want to play a character who is made(lineage) who's going to do these sorts of things(refinment). The Character then you know does Refinement sort of things. Gets quest rewards and gets new stuff. Or player decides they want to do other Refinementy things and goes off and does that. There's not really any particular demanded focus except what the player brings to it. Just like the Ghost wolf who doesn't want to play werewolf is a shit character a Promethean who's interpretation of the refinement they want to play that's at odd with the game is a shit character.<br /> <br /> So I as an ST say &quot;hey friends I want to run a full crossover CoD game.. except mummies,demons and hunters because fuck you that's why&quot; Someone who shows up with a &quot;I want to play a promethean on the refinment of copper who lives in the woods and won't interact with anyone&quot; is a shit character, he'd also be a shit character as a normal promethean game but an excellent npc and something that could easily exist in setting. When the players come back with &quot;A promethean on the Refinement of Silver&quot; A Beast and a Mage, its really really easy. Other groupings get progressiely harder but really Promethean things are 'have adventures and learn from them&quot; they are perhaps the most explicitly &quot;be a pc&quot; splat they just have a place to go when the game ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T01:39:11-08:00","id":800391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800368#post800368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethean doesn't give you that option, though. The pilgrimage is built into the mechanics of how prometheans work.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is built into the mechanics, but how is it built into the mechanics in a way that punishes a character for not striving for it? What's the stick that's beating you back? Centimanus isn't something that gets forced onto characters and isn't really a mechanical drawback anyway if you're not trying to progress on the Pilgrimage. There's no rule that makes you adopt a Pandoran pet and compulsively graft arms onto yourself. You don't lose Transmutations or Azoth for turning your back on the Pilgrimage, unless I'm forgetting something from the 2e spoilers. The Morality/Integrity trait exists, but I have a hard time seeing it as a severe burden for a character whose player doesn't mind being distanced from the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, there are goodies like vitriol you won't get if you're not progressing. Prometheans are hardly dependent on vitriol to be effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T04:13:40-08:00","id":800506,"title":"","content":"Okay, let me take a moment to step back and ask this question of you, Some Guy With a Katana. You don' t want a Promethean on a Pilgrimage. Okay, sure. Let me ask you this, then. What do you want out of the game? I enjoy taking games, basically rewriting them, and running them. I put the work into rewriting Mummy and its history to have less Egypt in it for a chronicle. I've played Prommies who's only goal in their half-life existance was to be a city's guardian angel, ala the Gargoyle's cartoon. We can tweak and make lots of suggestions, but only if we have some actual meat to bite into. So far, all I'm seeing is that you don't like the Pilgrimage. I don't really care about why you don't like it; that's immaterial. I just care what you do want out of the game.<br /> <br /> So, then, what do you want out of the game? We can work with that. We can't work with dislike of something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T04:37:25-08:00","id":800514,"title":"","content":"You could also repurpose the new dawn as a way to &quot;refine&quot;, &quot; distill&quot; or &quot;purify&quot; Azoth so that it no longer causes Disquiet, Wasteland or Torment. You will still be using the same mechanics, you will preserve the theme, and you won't have angry fans saying you're ignoring a core component of the game. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T05:34:15-08:00","id":800530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800514#post800514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also repurpose the new dawn as a way to &quot;refine&quot;, &quot; distill&quot; or &quot;purify&quot; Azoth so that it no longer causes Disquiet, Wasteland or Torment. You will still be using the same mechanics, you will preserve the theme, and you won't have angry fans saying you're ignoring a core component of the game. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><b>ShadowKnight</b>, you are personal robbed by me - I'm making this as mine own Hack for Transhuman prometheans I was writing before when 2ED comes in for it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T05:36:57-08:00","id":800532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800506#post800506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, let me take a moment to step back and ask this question of you, Some Guy With a Katana. You don' t want a Promethean on a Pilgrimage. Okay, sure. Let me ask you this, then. What do you want out of the game? I enjoy taking games, basically rewriting them, and running them. I put the work into rewriting Mummy and its history to have less Egypt in it for a chronicle. I've played Prommies who's only goal in their half-life existance was to be a city's guardian angel, ala the Gargoyle's cartoon. We can tweak and make lots of suggestions, but only if we have some actual meat to bite into. So far, all I'm seeing is that you don't like the Pilgrimage. I don't really care about why you don't like it; that's immaterial. I just care what you do want out of the game.<br /> <br /> So, then, what do you want out of the game? We can work with that. We can't work with dislike of something.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I see Promethean, what I see is a game about being an outsider. You're told, from the beginning, that there's no place for you in this world. You're an outcast, a reject, etc. To me, the game should be about trying to find how your character will deal with that. When you're told from your earliest memories that you're a mistake or something inferior, how do you handle that?<br /> <br /> The pilgrimage is one response. It's a perfectly valid response. What you are is unacceptable to the universe, so you try to change yourself to fit the world. But it's not the only way to go about things. Some people may try to carve out a place for themselves, to find a place that can accept them as they are. Some people become rebels. You don't accept me as I am? Fuck you then.<br /> <br /> Like I said before, I don't dislike the pilgrimage. I like it as one option of many. If I had the choice, I would not remove it from the game. But I would make it, as a whole, one of the social factions for prometheans, with the individual refinements as subsects, similar to Werewolf lodges. Then I'd have other groups for Prometheans who have chosen some other path. Off the top of my head, some thing kind of like an Ordo Dracul for Prometheans (Instead of becoming human, become a better monster.) whose transmutations would be all about trying to control and lessen the negative aspects of being a promethean. Then some obviously evil group that are a bunch of social darwinist/wannabe nietzche's who think prometheans are actually the ubermensch and they wanna rule the world or something. Like I said, these are just spinning out of my brain right now, and I haven't put much thought into them, but they're just examples of what I'm going for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T05:44:02-08:00","id":800537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800530#post800530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>ShadowKnight</b>, you are personal robbed by me - I'm making this as mine own Hack for Transhuman prometheans I was writing before when 2ED comes in for it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to hear! Glad I could help. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T06:12:31-08:00","id":800543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800532#post800532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I see Promethean, what I see is a game about being an outsider. You're told, from the beginning, that there's no place for you in this world. You're an outcast, a reject, etc. To me, the game should be about trying to find how your character will deal with that. When you're told from your earliest memories that you're a mistake or something inferior, how do you handle that?<br /> <br /> The pilgrimage is one response. It's a perfectly valid response. What you are is unacceptable to the universe, so you try to change yourself to fit the world. But it's not the only way to go about things. Some people may try to carve out a place for themselves, to find a place that can accept them as they are. Some people become rebels. You don't accept me as I am? Fuck you then.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, fair enough. However, you're still talking about a -rejection- of things. You don't like the path of obtaining mortality, and you're not looking to go into Flux. What would such a character actually -do-? That's what I'm stuck on. You are talking about things you don't want to do. I'm not entirely sure what's left here. Reject both paths, and... go off into the desert alone? Its doable; in fact, that's what the Copper refinement does. But, again, you don't want that, since its part of the Pilgrimage. Same with just indulging your base desires - Tin and Cobalt do that. How is your approach different from those? <br /> <br /> What does your &quot;fuck you world!&quot; approach entail? You build this character, following your own path. What would your Aspirations and goals and ambitions be? I really don't understand what you're asking for here. Given your words below, I'm coming to the conclusion that you're just unhappy with the end game situation, and not actually play styles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like I said before, I don't dislike the pilgrimage. I like it as one option of many. If I had the choice, I would not remove it from the game. But I would make it, as a whole, one of the social factions for prometheans, with the individual refinements as subsects, similar to Werewolf lodges. </div> </div> </div> Perhaps the simplist solution would be to change the end-goal of the different Refinements? Each Refinement is a path towards the Great Work. Aurum reflects becoming a human by mimicking, changing to fit humanity. The path of Torment is about your base desires and living as you will. I remember someone in the past suggested that Mercury would transform you into an angel/quashmal. Etc. Its a simple and elegant solution to your question. Would that work for what you want?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Off the top of my head, some thing kind of like an Ordo Dracul for Prometheans (Instead of becoming human, become a better monster.) whose transmutations would be all about trying to control and lessen the negative aspects of being a promethean. </div> </div> </div> Tin has these Transmutations actually. I've always thought of Tin as &quot;Flux lite.&quot; The Refinement of Tin focuses on understanding and controlling your Torment, and, by extension, Wastelands and Disquiet. Torment is, by defintion, the imbalanced Flux inherant within the Promethean. So, its basically a non-evil way of studying your monstrous nature and controlling it. Meanwhile, Cobalt studies sin and indulgence and other base desires for someone who wants to go that route. Actually, both Colbalt and Tin study Disquietism, which controls the monstrous nature parts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then some obviously evil group that are a bunch of social darwinist/wannabe nietzche's who think prometheans are actually the ubermensch and they wanna rule the world or something. </div> </div> </div> Actually, this last one is Centimani, flat out, no change needed. They're the Promethean equivalent to the cackling necromancer overlord wannabe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T06:51:14-08:00","id":800555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800386#post800386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's that it's exceedingly hard to come up with any reason why my created would, while trying to pursue the understanding of humanity, would be drawn to spending his time with a bunch of creatures which are decidedly not human.</div> </div> </div> </div>He can be honest with them in a way he can't be with humans. He can get outsider perspectives on humanity distinct from those of Prometheans. He can have a break (being on the Pilgrimmage doesn't mean everything you do 24/7 must be directed to that end). He can get help against torch-wielding mobs, or even help defusing things before they get to that point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800543#post800543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the simplist solution would be to change the end-goal of the different Refinements? Each Refinement is a path towards the Great Work. Aurum reflects becoming a human by mimicking, changing to fit humanity. The path of Torment is about your base desires and living as you will. I remember someone in the past suggested that Mercury would transform you into an angel/quashmal. Etc. Its a simple and elegant solution to your question. Would that work for what you want?</div> </div> </div> </div>Copper might be the purification option, the purging of Promethean weaknesses while retaining the strengths - Iron might be the one about reconciling how you are you now and making the best of it - they could work the other way round as well, depending on what you want to emphasise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 01-04-2016, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T06:55:46-08:00","id":800559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800543#post800543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps the simplist solution would be to change the end-goal of the different Refinements? Each Refinement is a path towards the Great Work. Aurum reflects becoming a human by mimicking, changing to fit humanity. The path of Torment is about your base desires and living as you will. I remember someone in the past suggested that Mercury would transform you into an angel/quashmal. Etc. Its a simple and elegant solution to your question. Would that work for what you want?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I would gladly read about those in context of &quot;New Dawn&quot; Hack the Shadow Knight proposed. Probably will start diffrent topic for this, as this will surely be non-canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T07:37:30-08:00","id":800572,"title":"","content":"Where's my delete button? It disappeared!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T13:40:24-08:00","id":800716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800514#post800514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also repurpose the new dawn as a way to &quot;refine&quot;, &quot; distill&quot; or &quot;purify&quot; Azoth so that it no longer causes Disquiet, Wasteland or Torment. You will still be using the same mechanics, you will preserve the theme, and you won't have angry fans saying you're ignoring a core component of the game. :P</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't see how this is a hack? I mean eventually you're going to want to end the game some how or it just drifts away. The new Dawn seems little different than the sadness that eventually your vampire or werewolf is just going to die. Its just an end game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T14:56:02-08:00","id":800757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800716#post800716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how this is a hack? I mean eventually you're going to want to end the game some how or it just drifts away. The new Dawn seems little different than the sadness that eventually your vampire or werewolf is just going to die. Its just an end game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all stories end when the main character dies or is fundamentally transformed. In fact, I'd say &quot;he retires somewhere peaceful&quot; to be a perfectly good ending for a character. Or &quot;she goes to travel the world/Shadow/etc.&quot; Or &quot;he goes into stasis/slumber, to be awakened in the future when X happens.&quot; Or &quot;she becomes the ruler of this area for Y years, and then hands over the position to her hand-picked heiress.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are many different endings that can work with a Promethean staying a non-human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T16:38:36-08:00","id":800805,"title":"","content":"And all of them clash with \u201cyou are on fire\u201d. That is, they all presuppose that the Promethean condition is one with which a reasonable person could be content. The premise of the game as written is that there is something horribly wrong with the Created \u2014 not \u201cyou're an outsider\u201d, which is more about being ostracized for being different, but something fundamentally and objectively broken and/or missing in the Promethean's nature. Changing that is, by definition, a hack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T17:06:53-08:00","id":800815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in the mechanics rulebook says that the society-eschewing vampire or the ghost wolf are going to get screwed over and have to fall into line eventually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I think you're wrong about Werewolves. Ignoring a hunt is a breaking point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">nWoD/CoD is supposed to be super-modular.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...mod it. I'm sorry the game isn't what you wanted but that's why it is so toolboxy. There's things I don't like about my favorite games, too, and maybe they'd be different were I in charge but I love them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if the only option for the guy who's given up on that goal is a batshit centimani, then it becomes a question of why any of those guys would wanna hang out with the 8-armed lunatic cackling like a maniac</div> </div> </div> </div>Second Edition for Promethean, judging by the previews, seems to have the Centimanni occupy a niche other than batshit eight-armed lunatic. It reminds me about someone saying they wanted to make Extempore a more consistent Lineage, which defeats the point of Extempore: to the a catch-all umbrella term for Prometheans existing without a Lineage. Likewise, Centimanni, I think, will become more of just the phrase for those Prometheans who act without the Pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> The Refinements, as MCN has wonderfully pointed out, aren't founded on &quot;How do we get to humanity?&quot; but &quot;How do we react to our existence?&quot; To me, though, you should just play a Centimanni. They don't <i>have</i> to be evil cackling overlords - at least I think that's the design change for second edition - but there's plenty of room in the Refinements.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, ask yourself what does it mean for the story of the settings? Run a campaign where, in a world of Prometheans on the Pilgrimage, there's a non-Centimannus who's figured out how to still neglect the Pilgrimage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T17:15:00-08:00","id":800821,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that in 2e, the Integrity substitute is \u201cPilgrimage\u201d. Think about the implications of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T17:27:34-08:00","id":800835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800805#post800805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The premise of the game as written is that there is something horribly wrong with the Created \u2014 not \u201cyou're an outsider\u201d, which is more about being ostracized for being different, but something fundamentally and objectively broken and/or missing in the Promethean's nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the assimilationist reading seems to invariably conclude that the Promethean state of dissatisfaction is internalized rather than <i>ab initio</i> internal, which, as I've pointed out in the other threads, ignores the facts of Torment alongside lower-key problems like rebellious organs and the lack of prior experience to unlearn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T18:28:34-08:00","id":800862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800757#post800757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not all stories end when the main character dies or is fundamentally transformed. In fact, I'd say &quot;he retires somewhere peaceful&quot; to be a perfectly good ending for a character. Or &quot;she goes to travel the world/Shadow/etc.&quot; Or &quot;he goes into stasis/slumber, to be awakened in the future when X happens.&quot; Or &quot;she becomes the ruler of this area for Y years, and then hands over the position to her hand-picked heiress.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are many different endings that can work with a Promethean staying a non-human.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not all stories do but the focus on the New Dawn here is like a focus on the fact that eventually you're werewolf is going to die in combat. There is no dying of old age only slowing down. Given enough time eventually your vampire will say the wrong thing and he will die. The only ending they have for their personal history is death. You can quit playing them with other &quot;last stories&quot; but the same is true with a promethean.<br /> <br /> Prometheans like Mages just happen to have a happy ending last story built in as a possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T20:10:49-08:00","id":800907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800862#post800862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">eventually you're werewolf is going to die in combat.<br /> <br /> our vampire will say the wrong thing and he will die.<br /> <br /> The only ending they have for their personal history is death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everybody dies.<br /> <br /> Even the Promethean that becomes a human after his New Dawn will die.<br /> <br /> Doesn't really change anything whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T20:17:08-08:00","id":800919,"title":"","content":"To be Fair I had a Player in a Brief WTA game I ran that wanted to run an ATHIEST charachter who sneered at environmentalism and was NOT happy at the game giving NO SUPPORT to such BS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T20:24:37-08:00","id":800929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800907#post800907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everybody dies.<br /> <br /> Even the Promethean that becomes a human after his New Dawn will die.<br /> <br /> Doesn't really change anything whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Redeemed is not likely to die still entangled with monsters and/or a supernatural force that will consume them if they fail to pursue enlightenment.<br /> <br /> The Hunt is never over and the Requiem carries on into eternity; grasping the Dawn means nobody and nothing is going to begrudge you your escape from the lake of fire you were half-born into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T05:19:19-08:00","id":801291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800929#post800929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Redeemed is not likely to die still entangled with monsters and/or a supernatural force that will consume them if they fail to pursue enlightenment.<br /> <br /> The Hunt is never over and the Requiem carries on into eternity; grasping the Dawn means nobody and nothing is going to begrudge you your escape from the lake of fire you were half-born into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people aren't into that, and I think it's perfectly valid to give them the tools they need to tinker with the game so that they can play the stories they want to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T05:38:37-08:00","id":801298,"title":"","content":"Oh, certainly. But don't expect any <i> official </i> support along those lines, and don't be surprised if you have to do extensive tinkering to get around the built-in assumptions that Satchel is describing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T05:40:58-08:00","id":801299,"title":"","content":"But what kind of story does he want to play? OP's 'alternatives' to the Pilgrimage were just descriptions of Refinements.<br /> <br /> I think <b>Promethean</b> by way of katanas and trenchcoats (if that's an option he's interested in) would be cool as much as the next guy but I don't need a book on how to do it. If that's the case I'm not sure why it has to be <b>Promethean</b> and not another game with better fitting mechanics where you just <i>say</i> someone created you in a lab. Anyway, in that kind of game you're going to be ignoring any splat's Integrity trait anyway, which is perfectly fine for this game considering it's <i>called</i> Pilgrimage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T05:57:02-08:00","id":801307,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Deviant will solve this problem. It wouldn't be too terribly difficult to make certain Deviants undead (borrowing some parts of Vampire and Mummy's templates) or even taking the physical advantages of Prometheans, and using that system to run such a chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:14:36-08:00","id":801319,"title":"","content":"Yeah; switching to a game with themes that better match your expectations is probably a smart move; and I think Deviant could indeed scratch the itch in question. As near as I can tell, it doesn't feature the \u201ctranscend my current state of being\u201d aspect that some find so troubling about Promethean \u2014 although I could see it including an option for \u201cI never wanted these powers; take them back!\u201d which is remarkably similar to the \u201cI want to become human!\u201dthing that Promethean features.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-05T06:35:15-08:00","id":801339,"title":"","content":"Deviant doesn't approach what's happened to the characters the same way Promethean does, because it draws from different sources - the Cronenburg-esque body horror of &quot;what's happened to me?&quot; rather than Promethean's &quot;what am I?&quot; Where you can mistake Promethean's work-in-progress protagonists as supporting transhumanism, Deviant's central conflict is set up differently.<br /> <br /> But at it's heart, Deviant says &quot;changing humans into monsters against their will is wrong,&quot; and explores what happens to the people who are changed anyway. That's not very transhumanist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-06T16:09:20-08:00","id":802410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/800278-more-options-for-prometheans-not-on-a-pilgrimage?p=800805#post800805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u201cyou are on fire\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering how long it was going to take for someone to use that line in this thread. So, that line seems like a good enough segue into the Idea I had earlier today: A Promethean Demi-Splat, called either Fire-Touched or Torchbearers.(not sure which I like better, also not sure one or both names aren't used elsewhere in CofD)<br /> Basically, they would be an option for Prometheans who don't hate <i>EVERYTHING</i> about being Prometheans, they just want to be something more stable; Promethean Lite, if you will. Here's my notes so far:<br /> <br /> They would be Redeemed, but not every Promethean would become one, this may be tied to what refinement they are on at the time of the New Dawn.<br /> Regaining Pyros might be harder, they might not have their own internal Azoth.<br /> Disquiet only happens when they use their Transmutations in front of witnesses, similar to how Vulgar effects with Sleeper witnesses upped the risk of Paradox in M:tAW 1ed; use of Transmutations reveals their Supernatural nature.(there would be exceptions, IIRC some transmutations are more subtle/don't cause a Promethean's Disfigurements to show.)<br /> The Lineage they used to belong to would still mark them in some way, just not as severe as a Prometheans' Disfigurements.<br /> They would not create the Wasteland effect, or it would be WAY slower; measured in months or years, rather than hours and days.<br /> They probably would not retain their Bestowments; but could retain the Boons of whatever Athanor they had when they went through the New Dawn.<br /> They retain memories of their Pilgrimage.<br /> Unaffected by Disquiet, Unseen Sense: Promethean merit.<br /> Torment might still be an issue, maybe not as bad.<br /> Still probably awaken/attract Pandorans, so maybe they <b>DO</b> still have Azoth.<br /> Not sure about electricity healing them.<br /> <br /> I welcome any thoughts on this idea, except for shitting all over it. There <u>IS</u> a difference between constructive criticism and being a dick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T20:46:57-08:00","id":803550,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I'll admit I'm not entirely on-board with the idea of a post-Redemption Promethean-Lite, but if you <i>were</i> to tinker with it further, &quot;Torchbearer&quot; feels more appropriate - they're carrying some small amount of the Divine Fire forward into their new lives, after all. Not enough to scorch the land around them, but enough to risk burning themselves and others.<br /> <br /> They'd absolutely need to have a diminished ability to store Pyros - a limit of either one of their Resistance attributes (Stamina is kind of a default, but there's an argument to be made for Resolve too), or that attribute + 5. As far as recovery options? Well... I think it'd be fair to at least let them keep the &quot;gain a point if outside during a thunderstorm&quot; thing, since it's mostly beyond their control and not very safe. Since they don't belong to their old Lineage anymore though, the &quot;sleep near their element&quot; thing should probably be dropped, as should the &quot;hanging out with people&quot; thing and... hmm. While dropping the &quot;one per day&quot; method might make it extremely difficult to accumulate (which to be fair would make sense, since Pyros Really Isn't A Thing Mortals Should Handle), keeping it seems a little too lenient. Maybe once a week at most, to encourage them to seek more... risky sources.<br /> <br /> I'd personally opt to have them respond to electricity (or radiation, if they're an ex-Zeka who somehow managed to survive their own fallout) the same way any other person off the street does, more or less. Maaaybe give them access to a merit that gives them some amount of &quot;armor&quot; against it at most. Of course, they'd still be allowed to generate Pyros with Electroshock Recharge if they have it... they'd just take the damage as well, ignoring whatever protection they may or may not have against frying themselves. They chose to keep playing with Fire, after all...<br /> <br /> (An aside, since they're not Prometheans anymore, using Sublimate Phlogiston to generate Pyros would actually be slightly less risky than before, since the overflow of damage would &quot;only&quot; be lethal for them. Between that and Electroshock Recharge, a Torchy would probably wind up with a lot of burn scars before long.)<br /> <br /> Might want to restrict whatever Transmutations they can learn to whatever two sets were relevant to the Refinement they were on when they Redeemed, plus one or two &quot;universal&quot; ones. Having the full list to choose from seems too good for someone who's approximately mortal, even with the restrictions on how they get their fuel.<br /> <br /> Yyyeah, definitely no Bestowments. Maybe they could Redeem with a supernatural merit reflecting whatever Bestowment they were born with though, or one they favored on the Pilgrimage. That could serve pretty well as an echo of their own Lineage as well, for bonus points.<br /> <br /> In agreement with the &quot;awaken and attract Pandorans&quot; bit, though probably only at the same level an Azoth 1 Prommie does, or at a level proportional in some way to the amount of Pyros they currently have.<br /> <br /> If you decide to play around with it a bit more, it probably wouldn't hurt to start a new thread for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":"01-09-2016, 01:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}